\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Choosing your photos\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Open 
\f0\b Photos-Go-Round -> Settings\'85
\f1\b0 .\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For albums in Photos, click 
\f0\b Select Collections\'85
\f1\b0 . The first time, click 
\f0\b Allow Access\'85
\f1\b0 , and macOS will ask whether Photos-Go-Round may read your photo library.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
For photos on disk, click 
\f0\b Add Picture Folder\'85
\f1\b0  or 
\f0\b Add Picture Files\'85
\f1\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
To see your Photos on your desktop, select \'93
\f0\b Photos-Go-Round Wallpaper
\f1\b0 \'94 from 
\f0\b System Settings
\f1\b0  -> 
\f0\b Wallpaper
\f1\b0 . To see your Photos when the screensaver starts, select \'93
\f0\b Photos-Go-Round Screensaver\'94
\f1\b0  from 
\f0\b System Settings
\f1\b0  -> 
\f0\b Wallpaper
\f1\b0  -> 
\f0\b Screensaver
\f1\b0 . Note that you will have to scroll all of the way to the bottom of available screensavers, and hit the \'93Other\'94 button, and \'93Show more\'94 to find it.\
To see your Photos in a widget, right-click the desktop, choose 
\f0\b Edit Widgets\'85
\f1\b0 , and pick 
\f0\b Photos-Go-Round
\f1\b0 . It comes in every size, and each widget shows a new photo every few minutes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Uninstalling\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf0 Open 
\f0\b Uninstall Photos-Go-Round
\f1\b0  from this disk image. It removes the app from Applications, the Photos-Go-Round Service, the wallpaper, the screensaver, the widgets, and your Photos-Go-Round settings. Your photographs themselves are not touched.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa331\partightenfactor0

